  "description": "One Cooper Flagg card sold for 8.04 million dollars. He's only 19.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Cooper Flagg: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cooper_Flagg\n\nFrom Wikipedia (Cooper Flagg): born in Newport, Maine; his mother Kelly played college basketball at the University of Maine and was team captain as a senior; the Dallas Mavericks picked him first overall in the 2025 NBA draft; on April 3, 2026 he scored a career-high 51 points, becoming the youngest player in NBA history to score 50+ (19 years and 103 days) and the first teenager to do it; he won the 2025-26 Rookie of the Year award; on September 25, 2026, his NBA Rookie Debut Patch Autograph card sold for $8.04 million through Fanatics Collect (ESPN, cited on the page). Not investment advice. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #cooperflagg #nba #howtheymakemoney",
